a \n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=\\frac{7}{8}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $sin⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{8}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{7}{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{49}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the positive answer since $sin⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So our final answer is $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c73db44-2ec2-5025-9431-acb02e414916" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Trigonometric Ratio Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a32365c-3ae5-53ac-a149-f47a33daf7c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511683} {:answer/id #uuid "931680d4-ddc2-5fe3-a179-0b349fd50d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{38}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511700} {:answer/id #uuid "ab910f87-b9dc-573a-978e-cb0375562e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{76}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511703} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f2325b-f13b-5140-9d7e-7661e658a40f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511709} {:answer/id #uuid "f4058ccc-66d9-56ac-a956-faf95687a1e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "931680d4-ddc2-5fe3-a179-0b349fd50d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/val